1
00:00:18,458 --> 00:00:23,417
There are likely no Titans among
the 104th Cadet Corps recruits!

2
00:00:23,417 --> 00:00:26,875
Multiple Titans from the south!

3
00:00:26,875 --> 00:00:29,917
Wall Rose has been breached!

4
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:41,083
The 104th Cadet Corps were kept isolated
under suspicion of Titans within their ranks.

5
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:49,208
But with the sudden appearance of Titans,
couriers were dispatched to warn each district.

6
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,042
As you may know,

7
00:00:54,042 --> 00:00:57,458
today marks the new darkest day
in humanity's history!

8
00:00:57,458 --> 00:01:03,500
If ever humankind needed
to give its all, that time is now!

9
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:04,833
However...

10
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:10,958
What?!

11
00:01:10,958 --> 00:01:12,792
They all started sprinting!

12
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:19,625
The cause of this crisis remains in the dark.

13
00:01:19,625 --> 00:01:22,167
For now, no one yet knows.

14
00:01:29,958 --> 00:01:34,542
I must say, what a clever idea.

15
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:17,000
"I'm Home"

16
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:21,667
"Trost District"

17
00:03:21,667 --> 00:03:23,958
Commander Pyxis!

18
00:03:23,958 --> 00:03:26,083
Titans have been spotted!

19
00:03:26,083 --> 00:03:29,417
Wall Rose has been breached!

20
00:03:30,625 --> 00:03:32,042
Hmm.

21
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:36,042
"Stohess District"

22
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:41,500
What the hell does all this mean?

23
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,333
Damn it!

24
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:44,458
But...

25
00:03:46,042 --> 00:03:50,250
Would Titans break walls with Titans in them?

26
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:54,625
It's happened before.
They busted the wall into our city.

27
00:03:54,625 --> 00:03:56,583
That was a gate.

28
00:03:58,333 --> 00:04:01,375
Armin? What are you saying?

29
00:04:01,375 --> 00:04:03,458
The thing about the walls...

30
00:04:03,458 --> 00:04:08,083
There's no crevices between the rocks
or any signs of cracking.

31
00:04:08,083 --> 00:04:11,167
We can't really tell how they're made.

32
00:04:13,083 --> 00:04:16,583
So what if they're made of hardened Titan skin?

33
00:04:18,833 --> 00:04:23,208
It must be pretty versatile
if Annie can encase herself.

34
00:04:25,250 --> 00:04:28,542
Titans... in the wall...

35
00:04:29,583 --> 00:04:32,417
Section Commander! What are you doing?

36
00:04:32,417 --> 00:04:34,708
We're supposed to leave in 5 minutes!

37
00:04:34,708 --> 00:04:35,792
Please hurry up!

38
00:04:35,792 --> 00:04:38,542
There's something I need to confirm--

39
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,667
Hey.

40
00:04:43,667 --> 00:04:44,708
Get moving.

41
00:04:44,708 --> 00:04:46,417
Ah, sorry!

42
00:04:46,417 --> 00:04:47,542
What about him?

43
00:04:47,542 --> 00:04:50,042
He's been ready for a while now.

44
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,542
Eren. Wear it right.

45
00:05:00,542 --> 00:05:02,333
It's cold at night.

46
00:05:02,333 --> 00:05:04,667
Sorry to keep ya!

47
00:05:04,667 --> 00:05:07,542
Took longer to prepare than we thought.

48
00:05:12,958 --> 00:05:14,500
Um...

49
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:17,583
Isn't this a priest from the Order of the Walls?

50
00:05:17,583 --> 00:05:20,583
Yeah. Nick and I are best buddies.

51
00:05:20,583 --> 00:05:22,333
Right?

52
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:24,542
Don't let him bother you.

53
00:05:24,542 --> 00:05:28,125
The whole makeup of this squad
doesn't make any sense.

54
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:30,167
Does it, Levi?

55
00:05:30,167 --> 00:05:32,750
No, I think it might.

56
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:35,917
Erwin picked them out for a reason.

57
00:05:35,917 --> 00:05:37,500
Open the gate!

58
00:05:46,125 --> 00:05:49,000
The situation within Wall Rose is unclear.

59
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,625
But everything up until Ehrmich is safe.

60
00:05:51,625 --> 00:05:53,875
We'll save time going through there.

61
00:05:53,875 --> 00:05:54,958
Move out!

62
00:05:54,958 --> 00:05:56,125
Yes, sir!

63
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:58,750
Take us out.

64
00:05:58,750 --> 00:05:59,833
Yes, sir!

65
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:20,125
This whole time, Titans have been
protecting us from Titans.

66
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,792
Huh? He knew?

67
00:06:33,792 --> 00:06:38,042
There's Titans inside the walls
and he's known about it?!

68
00:06:38,042 --> 00:06:40,458
Yes, though...

69
00:06:40,458 --> 00:06:43,667
...he's kept his mouth shut this entire time.

70
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:50,167
But now he's coming with us
to witness the harsh reality.

71
00:06:50,167 --> 00:06:54,042
Will his beliefs be strong enough
for him to stay silent?

72
00:06:54,042 --> 00:06:58,833
Or will seeing it with his own eyes
make him question himself?

73
00:06:58,833 --> 00:07:02,167
No, no, no, no! This is all backwards!

74
00:07:02,167 --> 00:07:05,250
If there's something you know, tell us about it!

75
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:09,792
Nothing's more important than
keeping humans from going extinct!

76
00:07:09,792 --> 00:07:12,417
Eren, settle down.

77
00:07:12,417 --> 00:07:14,500
You're still not fully healed.

78
00:07:15,542 --> 00:07:19,042
There's more than one way to get answers.

79
00:07:19,042 --> 00:07:25,167
I may be injured and useless right now,
but it doesn't take much to watch one man.

80
00:07:25,167 --> 00:07:30,417
I'm hoping we can settle this
without blasting a hole in anyone.

81
00:07:30,417 --> 00:07:31,625
Aren't you?

82
00:07:31,625 --> 00:07:33,875
Threatening him doesn't work, Levi.

83
00:07:33,875 --> 00:07:35,958
Believe me, I've tried.

84
00:07:35,958 --> 00:07:41,292
It seems to me that this priest
is capable of sound judgment.

85
00:07:41,292 --> 00:07:43,625
That's why I wonder...

86
00:07:43,625 --> 00:07:45,833
What if the reason he doesn't talk

87
00:07:45,833 --> 00:07:50,292
is because he knows something more
important than the fate of humanity?

88
00:07:53,417 --> 00:07:55,458
See that? It's the village!

89
00:07:55,458 --> 00:07:56,792
Is that the last one?

90
00:07:56,792 --> 00:08:00,833
No! My village is deep in the forest!

91
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:03,958
I'll go there alone!

92
00:08:03,958 --> 00:08:05,333
All right!

93
00:08:05,333 --> 00:08:07,458
Leave this village to me!

94
00:08:07,458 --> 00:08:08,625
Got it!

95
00:08:15,208 --> 00:08:17,958
Hey! Quit it, Sasha!

96
00:08:17,958 --> 00:08:21,667
Sasha! You been nabbing snacks again?!

97
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:23,292
Stop! Spit it out!

98
00:08:23,292 --> 00:08:24,750
Get it out of yer mouth!

99
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:28,458
We fixin' to smoke that for winter, ya moron!

100
00:08:38,375 --> 00:08:41,250
You damn dumb girl!

101
00:08:41,250 --> 00:08:43,000
Fine!

102
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,583
Have it yer way.

103
00:08:46,292 --> 00:08:47,708
Dagnabbit.

104
00:08:57,458 --> 00:08:58,833
Sasha.

105
00:08:58,833 --> 00:09:04,417
Have you asked yerself
why the world is a-changing?

106
00:09:04,417 --> 00:09:09,167
Why these past few years the forest
be shrinkin' and game harder to find?

107
00:09:09,167 --> 00:09:11,083
Have you ever thunk about it?

108
00:09:12,875 --> 00:09:17,750
It's 'cause more people be comin' and
taking food and game from the forest.

109
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:20,458
That's why I'm hungry.

110
00:09:20,458 --> 00:09:23,042
That's true.

111
00:09:23,042 --> 00:09:24,542
But, hey...

112
00:09:24,542 --> 00:09:30,167
They lost their homes and got no place to go.
They got no other choice.

113
00:09:30,167 --> 00:09:32,167
Their fault for losing it.

114
00:09:32,167 --> 00:09:34,375
They oughta leave ours.

115
00:09:35,667 --> 00:09:37,500
Titans took it from 'em.

116
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:42,625
They knocked a hole straight through Wall Maria.
Where else can they go?

117
00:09:43,792 --> 00:09:50,750
You can feed a hell of a lot more people
by clearin' the forest and plantin' grain.

118
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:59,208
Maybe it's time for our family to let go
of the forest and give up huntin' for good.

119
00:10:00,375 --> 00:10:06,042
The government said they would pay us.
Every horse that we raise is money in our pockets.

120
00:10:06,042 --> 00:10:07,792
You gotta be kidding!

121
00:10:07,792 --> 00:10:10,750
If we give up huntin',
we be givin' up who we are!

122
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:14,875
Why should we give a hoot about
the people who make fun of our lifestyle?

123
00:10:14,875 --> 00:10:16,417
I'll tell ya why.

124
00:10:18,167 --> 00:10:23,042
It's because... we're all
part of the same world.

125
00:10:23,042 --> 00:10:27,167
We humans... We've always been pack animals.

126
00:10:27,167 --> 00:10:30,042
Sure, we all live our different ways.

127
00:10:30,042 --> 00:10:35,500
But when space is this short, we gotta
join the group and do what's best to--

128
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,625
No! I refuse!

129
00:10:37,625 --> 00:10:42,083
We've lived here all our lives,
just like the way our ancestors taught us!

130
00:10:42,083 --> 00:10:45,042
We don't owe nothing to any outsiders!

131
00:10:49,583 --> 00:10:51,167
I see...

132
00:10:51,167 --> 00:10:53,167
So be it.

133
00:10:55,125 --> 00:11:01,208
Ya can live here in this forest,
along with the others who think the same.

134
00:11:02,417 --> 00:11:04,375
But, Sasha...

135
00:11:04,375 --> 00:11:07,625
Are ya willin' to die for that choice?

136
00:11:08,667 --> 00:11:13,625
No matter what trouble comes yer way,
ya can't go beggin' for help.

137
00:11:13,625 --> 00:11:19,708
If you're not there for them,
don't expect them to be there for you.

138
00:11:20,792 --> 00:11:26,125
I'm willin' to give up our traditions
if it means I can live with my family.

139
00:11:26,125 --> 00:11:30,417
Goes to show ya our world's connected,
whether you like it or not.

140
00:11:32,083 --> 00:11:37,167
Sasha. Are you that much of a scaredy-cat?

141
00:11:37,167 --> 00:11:44,042
Is it that hard for you to leave this forest
behind and get along with others?

142
00:11:47,875 --> 00:11:50,667
It's been 3 years since I've been back.

143
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:54,292
Surely he realized something
was amiss and fled...

144
00:11:58,083 --> 00:12:01,333
It can't be! Way out here?

145
00:12:03,917 --> 00:12:07,042
They've already come this far?!

146
00:12:08,458 --> 00:12:12,375
This place isn't safe for people anymore.

147
00:12:16,333 --> 00:12:20,417
What's that? A new village?

148
00:13:26,042 --> 00:13:31,042
"In addition to the cities at the walls, there exist
villages of various sizes contained within the walls."

149
00:13:40,750 --> 00:13:44,750
Damn! If I don't slice it off,
it'll just heal back up!

150
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,333
A child?

151
00:14:03,917 --> 00:14:06,333
I'm so sorry...

152
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:22,583
What's your name?

153
00:14:25,833 --> 00:14:27,958
Don't worry. It'll be okay.

154
00:14:27,958 --> 00:14:28,875
What will?

155
00:14:28,875 --> 00:14:32,125
Huh? What? I mean... Um...

156
00:14:33,292 --> 00:14:35,417
Steady... Steady...

157
00:14:35,417 --> 00:14:37,708
Um, you see...

158
00:14:37,708 --> 00:14:38,708
Huh?

159
00:14:39,708 --> 00:14:41,542
You're kidding me! Hey!

160
00:14:41,542 --> 00:14:43,750
Please wait for us!

161
00:14:46,125 --> 00:14:47,792
There's no need to worry.

162
00:14:47,792 --> 00:14:49,792
Please stay calm. It'll come right back.

163
00:14:49,792 --> 00:14:52,000
Why are you so nice when you talk?

164
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,167
What?

165
00:15:02,167 --> 00:15:03,667
Run away from here!

166
00:15:06,833 --> 00:15:08,375
It'll be okay!

167
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:13,250
Why? Everyone already left.

168
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:17,625
The whole village knew
my mother's legs were bad.

169
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,625
But not a single person came to help.

170
00:15:20,625 --> 00:15:22,750
All I could do was watch.

171
00:15:42,042 --> 00:15:43,708
It'll be okay!

172
00:15:47,083 --> 00:15:48,583
It's okay.

173
00:15:51,625 --> 00:15:53,917
You're really starting to tick me off.

174
00:15:53,917 --> 00:15:55,083
What?

175
00:15:55,083 --> 00:15:58,417
That stupid way you talk politely to everyone.

176
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,708
Why don't you talk to other cadets like normal?

177
00:16:02,708 --> 00:16:05,875
Um... Well, you see...

178
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,417
Wait. Let me guess.

179
00:16:09,417 --> 00:16:13,042
You're embarrassed by the way
people sound from your village.

180
00:16:13,042 --> 00:16:14,083
Bull's-eye?

181
00:16:14,083 --> 00:16:17,792
I'm surprised an idiot like you cares so much.

182
00:16:17,792 --> 00:16:23,875
You can't do anything but hunt,
and you're afraid of people, to top it off.

183
00:16:23,875 --> 00:16:27,833
I bet you don't have a single good reason
for aiming to become a soldier.

184
00:16:27,833 --> 00:16:29,083
Your parents probably--

185
00:16:29,083 --> 00:16:30,458
Stop it, Ymir! You're being--

186
00:16:30,458 --> 00:16:31,500
Sasha!

187
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:35,833
You gonna care what other people think
and be someone you're not your whole life?

188
00:16:35,833 --> 00:16:37,708
What a crock of shit.

189
00:16:37,708 --> 00:16:42,250
You're fine as is, so talk in
your own words for crying out loud.

190
00:16:44,083 --> 00:16:47,458
Th-Thank you...

191
00:16:47,458 --> 00:16:48,958
...very much.

192
00:16:48,958 --> 00:16:50,333
What?

193
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:51,833
I'm... sorry.

194
00:16:51,833 --> 00:16:53,708
I'm not... yet...

195
00:16:53,708 --> 00:16:55,375
Cut it out!

196
00:16:55,375 --> 00:16:59,042
There's nothing wrong with the way she talks!

197
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:03,042
Sasha is who Sasha wants to be.

198
00:17:03,042 --> 00:17:05,833
Her words will always be her own.

199
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:08,583
And I happen to like her.

200
00:17:08,583 --> 00:17:11,375
Hmph! Have it your way.

201
00:17:11,375 --> 00:17:16,417
Still, even if she changed the way she talks,
it won't change the fact that she's annoying.

202
00:17:16,417 --> 00:17:20,375
You know, not everyone is as insensitive as you.

203
00:17:20,375 --> 00:17:21,958
Excuse me?

204
00:17:21,958 --> 00:17:24,708
You little... You little...

205
00:17:25,917 --> 00:17:28,958
Hey! What are you laughing at?!

206
00:17:28,958 --> 00:17:31,500
Ah! I'm sorry!

207
00:17:37,750 --> 00:17:41,042
Why do I remember, now of all times...

208
00:17:41,042 --> 00:17:44,083
...about silly, pointless days in the past?

209
00:17:44,083 --> 00:17:47,708
It's all... I can think of.

210
00:17:50,125 --> 00:17:51,792
Hey, listen up.

211
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,417
You'll be fine. Keep following this path.

212
00:17:56,417 --> 00:17:58,500
Run as far as you can.

213
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:01,750
I promise someone will be there to help you.

214
00:18:01,750 --> 00:18:04,458
You might not find them right away...

215
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:08,000
But still, keep running until you do!

216
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,708
Now, go!

217
00:18:09,708 --> 00:18:11,083
Run!

218
00:18:14,750 --> 00:18:16,708
Get runnin'!

219
00:18:32,708 --> 00:18:36,583
If I take out both eyes,
it'll buy us plenty of time.

220
00:18:42,708 --> 00:18:44,792
Only... two left.

221
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,458
Relax...

222
00:18:47,458 --> 00:18:50,583
All it is... is a big...

223
00:18:50,583 --> 00:18:51,750
...slow moving...

224
00:18:51,750 --> 00:18:53,042
...target!

225
00:18:56,083 --> 00:18:57,125
Got it!

226
00:19:00,958 --> 00:19:02,667
One more arrow.

227
00:19:02,667 --> 00:19:05,833
But, if I miss this...

228
00:19:09,083 --> 00:19:11,042
...we can't escape.

229
00:19:11,042 --> 00:19:14,542
If I miss, me and...

230
00:19:14,542 --> 00:19:16,042
...that girl...

231
00:19:43,792 --> 00:19:46,542
I slipped out thanks to that blood.

232
00:19:46,542 --> 00:19:48,417
Now I've gotta find that girl!

233
00:19:54,125 --> 00:19:56,542
Huh? Sasha?

234
00:20:15,167 --> 00:20:19,125
We been givin' horses to everyone in the area.

235
00:20:19,125 --> 00:20:23,333
That girl told us someone was still back there.

236
00:20:23,333 --> 00:20:26,833
Who'da thunk it was you?

237
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:30,333
You fought off a Titan for that girl, didn't ya?

238
00:20:32,833 --> 00:20:35,708
Sasha... Yer all I hoped for.

239
00:20:37,792 --> 00:20:39,458
Father...

240
00:20:41,667 --> 00:20:43,167
I'm home.

241
00:20:47,083 --> 00:20:49,208
Conny, wait!

242
00:20:49,208 --> 00:20:50,583
Calm down!

243
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:53,167
There could be Titans anywhere!

244
00:20:53,167 --> 00:20:55,250
Get back here, Conny!

245
00:20:58,333 --> 00:20:59,667
This can't be...

246
00:21:04,458 --> 00:21:08,000
Anyone?! Is anyone there?!

247
00:21:09,417 --> 00:21:11,542
It's me! Conny!

248
00:21:11,542 --> 00:21:14,125
I came back!

249
00:21:23,083 --> 00:21:24,250
My house!

250
00:21:27,958 --> 00:21:29,833
Dad...

251
00:21:29,833 --> 00:21:31,208
Mom...

252
00:21:31,208 --> 00:21:34,250
Sunny... Martin!

253
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:36,625
Please be okay!

254
00:21:52,250 --> 00:21:54,958
Conny! Get back!

255
00:21:54,958 --> 00:21:58,333
It's... my house.

256
00:21:58,333 --> 00:21:59,917
My...

257
00:21:59,917 --> 00:22:01,625
Conny...

258
00:22:01,625 --> 00:22:03,292
Fall back, you two!

259
00:22:03,292 --> 00:22:05,000
I'll scout the area!

260
00:22:07,833 --> 00:22:10,333
Wait, it's...

261
00:22:10,333 --> 00:22:11,750
It can't move?

262
00:22:11,750 --> 00:22:13,750
Not with those legs...

263
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:19,167
Th-Then... How?

264
00:22:19,167 --> 00:22:21,500
How did it even get here?!

265
00:23:58,333 --> 00:24:01,417
"I'm sure my family is safe and sound."

266
00:24:01,417 --> 00:24:05,750
Shaking off the dread of Titans
appearing in his hometown,

267
00:24:05,750 --> 00:24:08,750
Conny once again departs.

268
00:24:08,750 --> 00:24:14,458
Battle erupts across the land
while the mystery of the Titans remains.

269
00:24:14,458 --> 00:24:17,000
As the plight worsens,

270
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:22,625
Eren and the others heading for Ehrmich District
receive a clue that might reveal the truth.

271
00:24:22,625 --> 00:24:27,179
Next episode: "Southwestward."
